WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.128 --> 00:00:02.148
- All I know about Danish is the pastry.

00:00:02.148 --> 00:00:06.639
(bouncy, upbeat music)

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.375
- [Voiceover] Aeblegrod.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.689
- Oh see, I never understood what

00:00:09.689 --> 00:00:11.974
the A combined with the E.

00:00:11.974 --> 00:00:12.775
- Eblegroom.

00:00:12.775 --> 00:00:13.948
- These are characters that I thought

00:00:13.948 --> 00:00:15.631
were just for shitz and gigs,

00:00:15.631 --> 00:00:17.616
like in the font category.

00:00:17.616 --> 00:00:18.649
- Iblegrood.

00:00:18.649 --> 00:00:19.753
- It's apricot.

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:20.728
- [Voiceover] Hakkebof.

00:00:20.728 --> 00:00:22.206
- Hockay.

00:00:22.206 --> 00:00:23.600
- It looks like Hasselhoff.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.226
- Hasselhoff.

00:00:24.226 --> 00:00:24.819
- Hakabeef

00:00:24.819 --> 00:00:25.665
- Hakaboof.

00:00:25.665 --> 00:00:27.546
- It's like it sounds
different every time.

00:00:27.546 --> 00:00:29.718
- It's its own Danish beef.

00:00:29.718 --> 00:00:31.422
- [Voiceover] Faedreland.

00:00:31.422 --> 00:00:32.678
- Faderland.

00:00:32.678 --> 00:00:33.966
- This sounds like a theme park,

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.266
Faydraland.

00:00:35.266 --> 00:00:36.045
- Fedrooland.

00:00:36.045 --> 00:00:37.101
- That was so awful.

00:00:37.101 --> 00:00:37.682
- That actually...

00:00:37.682 --> 00:00:39.086
That's a beautiful word.

00:00:39.086 --> 00:00:41.385
- [Voiceover] Paskesondagspraediken.

00:00:41.385 --> 00:00:43.637
- Presskondadangspradiken.

00:00:43.637 --> 00:00:44.717
- That's one word?

00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:46.041
- Oh!

00:00:46.041 --> 00:00:48.676
- Okay, Sondag is obviously Sunday.

00:00:48.676 --> 00:00:50.475
Puskasondagspradeeken.

00:00:50.475 --> 00:00:53.247
- Paskasondangspradaken.

00:00:53.247 --> 00:00:54.511
- Okay, I got like the first half.

00:00:54.511 --> 00:00:55.870
- Do Danish people open their mouths,

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:56.927
'cause I'm the complete opposite.

00:00:56.927 --> 00:00:58.424
- [Voiceover] Rodgrod Med Flode

00:00:58.424 --> 00:00:59.709
- Rogro Me Floo.

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:00.974
- Rodgrod Me Flod.

00:01:00.974 --> 00:01:02.252
- I'm not doing that badly.

00:01:02.252 --> 00:01:03.285
- Redgay Me Flay

00:01:03.285 --> 00:01:04.969
- This kind of reminds me of Calculus

00:01:04.969 --> 00:01:06.233
more than a language.

00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:07.534
- I feel like I'm correct

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.531
but I'm just saying it in an American way.

00:01:09.531 --> 00:01:11.059
- [Voiceover] Vidunderlig.

00:01:11.059 --> 00:01:12.235
- Vudunderling.

00:01:12.235 --> 00:01:13.013
- Videgerl...

00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:13.745
What? What?

00:01:13.745 --> 00:01:15.127
I'ma feel like I can get this one.

00:01:15.127 --> 00:01:15.812
- Vedooderling.

00:01:15.812 --> 00:01:17.559
- Vindunderlig.

00:01:17.559 --> 00:01:18.145
- You know what?

00:01:18.145 --> 00:01:19.109
They speak like Sims.

00:01:19.109 --> 00:01:19.945
The Sims.

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:21.384
- Okay, I added an extra N.

00:01:21.384 --> 00:01:22.092
- Vidunderlig.

00:01:22.092 --> 00:01:22.835
Oh, I got it.

00:01:22.835 --> 00:01:23.950
I mean, it's close enough.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:24.692
Vidunderlig.

00:01:24.692 --> 00:01:25.354
- That's pretty.

00:01:25.354 --> 00:01:26.968
That was a very pretty word.

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:28.930
- Wonderful. Vidunderlig!

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:30.904
- [Voiceover] Forarsjaevndogn.

00:01:30.904 --> 00:01:32.413
- Yep, don't know what the cirlce means.

00:01:32.413 --> 00:01:33.434
- I don't know what that little degree

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:34.410
is supposed to be.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.152
- Forsharshado.

00:01:35.152 --> 00:01:36.581
- There's that A and E.

00:01:36.581 --> 00:01:38.726
- Dyn, like "dynomite".

00:01:40.187 --> 00:01:41.820
- You have two letters in one letter,

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.422
if the word isn't long enough.

00:01:43.422 --> 00:01:44.537
- Very, very enlightening

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:45.860
just to see the types of sounds

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.264
other people can make.

00:01:47.264 --> 00:01:49.076
Like, I could never make
some of those sounds.

00:01:49.076 --> 00:01:50.318
- It was really, really difficult.

00:01:50.318 --> 00:01:51.618
- And it does sound like the Simsling,

00:01:51.618 --> 00:01:52.640
which I was right on that.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.998
- But when I heard how it was supposed

00:01:53.998 --> 00:01:55.865
to be pronounced, I couldn't even like

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:58.178
understand how it's
supposed to be pronounced.

00:01:58.178 --> 00:02:03.178
(bouncy, upbeat music)

